try><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia report hacking attacks on emergency alert apps</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9da686321f945716172d2e2c5c0697aa9110cf99135ff13b27e60bd92d2e45e</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:44Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T02:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-report-hacking-attacks-on-emergency-alert-apps/live-79825079--4c88f484410d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-report-hacking-attacks-on-emergency-alert-apps/live-79825079?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukraine and Russia have both reported cyberattacks targeting applications used to send emergency alerts to the public. Meanwhile, Zelenskyy said Ukraine will stop refinery strikes if the US sends Patriot missiles.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police investigating after needles found in Halloween candy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:143c294ffbe22e309b5dfb63c530a2f7fda677ef3509b4a8e416d516dddb51b8</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T01:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-investigating-after-needles-found-in-halloween-candy/a-79825051--00c6413d6c8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-investigating-after-needles-found-in-halloween-candy/a-79825051?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German police said they received phone calls with reports about sharp objects concealed in Halloween candy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's giant new radar in Kaliningrad raises alarm in NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8716a00f0746dcdfd0effcb6c676a6bbe41c75e3d282d6a26ce0e65d7f5d9cc5</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T20:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815--4cdeadba9801.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-giant-new-radar-in-kaliningrad-raises-alarm-in-nato/a-79797815?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia is nearing completion of what experts think is a giant radar complex in Kaliningrad, capable of monitoring much of Europe. Experts warn the project could intensify the military standoff between Moscow and NATO.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: Police chief arrested after election for abuse of office</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3d0caf57f639ad8767cc35604e9a6d3ed3322c471798895302c5081ba1f19686</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-police-chief-arrested-after-election-for-abuse-of-office/a-79823382--e5e7dbfa8fac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-police-chief-arrested-after-election-for-abuse-of-office/a-79823382?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Marko Kricak, an Aleksandar Vucic loyalist, is accused of suppressing and manipulating an investigation into a gangland murder. Prosecutors say the arrest is not linked to Vucic's recent election defeat.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France opens attempted murder probe after protest attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ab0f42d7bdff41ebfee8fb6b5c94c1ba1b2a2412de738cc8380942647ce0172</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T14:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-opens-attempted-murder-probe-after-protest-attack/a-79822853--daa7efa660e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-opens-attempted-murder-probe-after-protest-attack/a-79822853?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paris prosecutors have opened an attempted murder investigation after a Molotov attack on police. France reported 779 arrests during nationwide protests and Halloween night, fewer than on previous weekends.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Six-day localized ceasefire in Oleshky comes to end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c2dd4332e6c841d8ec640eebecad5a450752a8302d5c46ca105e234f712a542</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:28:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T14:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-six-day-localized-ceasefire-in-oleshky-comes-to-end/live-79815409--9508daa3ef0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-six-day-localized-ceasefire-in-oleshky-comes-to-end/live-79815409?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A US-brokered ceasefire in Ukraine's southern Kherson region ended on Sunday night with no violations reported. But Russian airstrikes continued in other parts of Ukraine.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ethnic Germans in Kazakhstan face legacy of the Soviet Union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e907e294316e50533a33aedd2251ae98bfa5df5e26dce4ff2b6941c38c427b1c</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T13:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048--09fc50df10b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethnic-germans-in-kazakhstan-face-legacy-of-the-soviet-union/a-79754048?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kazakhstan is struggling to deal with the legacy of the Soviet dictatorship. Some 85 years ago, Stalin deported hundreds of thousands of people: Some 400,000 ethnic Germans living in the USSR were sent to Kazakhstan.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Gen Z group calls for new protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ccf539311345cd9696a051f0e9226158bd57b65c76ebcd2180e4984392cbb26</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T12:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-gen-z-group-calls-for-new-protests/live-79814961--f0055b176099.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-gen-z-group-calls-for-new-protests/live-79814961?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The group behind German demonstrations this weekend has called for more protests to keep pressure on the government to act. Meanwhile, the IG Metall union has begun warning strikes after pay talks collapse. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Biological weapons: The weaponization of disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2e5b90de58eeace014cb433b867085f6d6365eb86b23af97f7500f8f55abe41</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T12:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/biological-weapons-the-weaponization-of-disease/a-79819662--554c8f7269e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/biological-weapons-the-weaponization-of-disease/a-79819662?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Biological weapons are prohibited under international law. But new developments in biotech and AI are a cause for concern. DW addresses some of the most important questions about their history, risks, and control.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal police storm housing protest camps in Lisbon, Porto</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11264c8d179d67712d47d49b34a7268f4459042d9e59be0fcf9c15f6c13e7722</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T11:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/portugal-police-storm-housing-protest-camps-in-lisbon-porto/a-79821643--43c94083971a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/portugal-police-storm-housing-protest-camps-in-lisbon-porto/a-79821643?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Clashes broke out as officers again dispersed housing protesters from tent camps in Lisbon and Porto. Portuguese police have repeatedly cleared tent camps erected across both cities in recent weeks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition holds major rally in Delhi over voter roll revisions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51f53f88ca9fd09dc7f3df68e8d9e35b4a3b598d45d428601dc06b3c569c6aeb</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T10:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-holds-major-rally-in-delhi-over-voter-roll-revisions/live-79820226--9ac26a00403b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-holds-major-rally-in-delhi-over-voter-roll-revisions/live-79820226?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands are expected to take part in the Indian opposition's planned mega march in New Delhi over a controversial revision of electoral rolls.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump loses allies after elections in Serbia and Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6cbb959aeb53951cd05a97c5174c6eea51f860ba414bbbdafea1361df3636322</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T08:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-loses-allies-after-elections-in-serbia-and-brazil/a-79812075--1fdc38eaf775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/donald-trump-loses-allies-after-elections-in-serbia-and-brazil/a-79812075?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro failed to gain power, Aleksandar Vucic was voted out of office, and even Benjamin Netanyahu's position has weakened. An unhappy US President Trump is crying electoral fraud.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's search for a nuclear waste site</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9befa4d796537593d9fe43fc42dbc59bd96d30721d8b6010617fe38e10897a56</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T08:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678--66cee2f12295.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-search-for-a-nuclear-waste-site/a-79820678?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Finland has become the first country with a final storage facility for nuclear waste. Germany is still searching for a site, while some countries have yet to start. Costs are expected to total many billions of euros.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>FBI says North Korea behind $6 billion Binance crypto theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef0d5c7b0c35222e092d8c0b9a7e8572a5e610c7e1ae1be101c65583f60b2980</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998--ddc7ca6650b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The FBI said the theft was tied to "malicious cyber activity" by an entity known as TraderTraitor, the same actors behind a $1.5 billion Bybit hack last year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bolivia declares emergency as El Nino intensifies, threatens severe weather</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ca0a98ba88fd207af50d1d956daf9b763b2b792cddac438509c61156d2981aa</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T06:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bolivia-declares-emergency-as-el-nino-intensifies-threatens-severe-weather/a-79820253--598e6e7adead.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bolivia-declares-emergency-as-el-nino-intensifies-threatens-severe-weather/a-79820253?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Rodrigo Paz warned of severe droughts and flooding as El Nino intensifies, with at least 78,000 families already affected by drought.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump grants visa to mother of Ghanaian boy killed in NYC — Mamdani</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbce5be5ef05de82b193b3ebdcce68607a459585e8fdb10150016982df9cb193</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T03:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-grants-visa-to-mother-of-ghanaian-boy-killed-in-nyc-mamdani/a-79820019--ed613f7f7bb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-grants-visa-to-mother-of-ghanaian-boy-killed-in-nyc-mamdani/a-79820019?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Javits Frimpong was on his way to school when he was shot in a neighborhood in the Bronx. He was 15 years old.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia after Vucic: The winners are losing patience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9803223e61abb39d32d569e4e3e814163f20d0f336a428ab6a5004e83b3286e</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586--7cebe42bf331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Student List's election victory, Aleksandar Vucic's power apparatus is disintegrating. People want justice as soon as possible. But the losers still hold sway in the judiciary and administration.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>More than 290 arrested in France as some weekend protests turn violent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5baf97c428fa83867710621904e49ea62e1a41163c89f07e5a3225fc1f77884e</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T18:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-than-290-arrested-in-france-as-some-weekend-protests-turn-violent/a-79818138--cf89bc00ce66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-than-290-arrested-in-france-as-some-weekend-protests-turn-violent/a-79818138?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protests continue across France as 320,000 people take to the streets over rising living costs and poor school conditions for a third consecutive weekend, with clashes reported in several cities.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Gen Z protests disrupted by violence on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75c196ac4810ed838a7a37433e4ede9730e2ae1846bcc19735501ff4cb461ec2</id><updated>2026-11-02T06:27:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694--76fbedb708ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nationwide protests led by young people were largely peaceful throughout the day, but reports about looting and rioting in the evening, especially in Frankfurt, overshadowed the spirit of the demonstrations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
